<h3 id="medic-icons">Medic Icons</h3>
<p>GymPress includes the Medic icon font. To show a medic icon, add its HTML to a <strong>Custom HTML</strong> widget, in any widget area or in the Page Builder. Use a class name from the list below:</p>
<p><code>&lt;i class="mp mp-ambulance-car"&gt;&lt;/i&gt;</code></p>
<p>To show a medic icon in a button, put the same HTML before the button text:</p>
<p><code>[button]&lt;i class="mp mp-ambulance-car"&gt;&lt;/i&gt; Contact us[/button]</code></p>
<p>Don't enter medic icons in a widget's icon field, in the <b>icon</b> attribute of <code>[fa]</code> or in the <b>fa</b> attribute of <code>[button]</code>. These add the Font Awesome class, and the medic icon doesn't display. The visual editor of the Text widget and the SiteOrigin Editor removes empty <code>&lt;i&gt;</code> tags, so use the Custom HTML widget.</p>
